('127.676.d.16.D',4,'Hiding an SSID is generally considered:','["the same as encryption", "weak security because the name can still be discovered", "unbreakable protection", "required by law"]'::jsonb,1,'Hidden names are easy to detect.','original'),
('127.676.d.16.E',3,'MAC spoofing is when an attacker:','["upgrades the router", "encrypts a drive", "falsifies a device''s hardware address to impersonate it", "prints a label"]'::jsonb,2,'Spoofing fakes identity.','original'),
('127.676.d.16.E',4,'An ''evil twin'' attack uses a fake wireless access point that:','["fixes weak signals", "increases speed", "blocks all devices", "imitates a legitimate network to capture user data"]'::jsonb,3,'Victims connect to the rogue network.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.A',3,'Application security focuses on:','["protecting software from threats throughout its life", "painting logos", "choosing office chairs", "designing keyboards"]'::jsonb,0,'AppSec covers the software lifecycle.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.A',4,'Security is best built into software:','["only after release", "from the start of design", "only after a breach", "never"]'::jsonb,1,'Early security is cheaper and stronger.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.B',3,'Reviewing code for security flaws before release is called:','["a font review", "a speed run", "a secure code review", "a screen test"]'::jsonb,2,'Reviews catch flaws early.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.B',4,'Using input validation and parameterized queries are examples of:','["hardware upgrades", "data loss", "marketing tactics", "secure coding practices"]'::jsonb,3,'They prevent injection attacks.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.C',3,'A vulnerability scanner is a tool that:','["checks systems for known weaknesses", "blocks all emails", "writes code for you", "cleans keyboards"]'::jsonb,0,'Scanners search for known flaws.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.C',4,'After a vulnerability scan, results are typically used to:','["delete the scanner", "prioritize and fix the discovered issues", "ignore high-risk items", "publish them online"]'::jsonb,1,'Findings drive remediation.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.D',3,'A buffer overflow occurs when a program:','["reads too little data", "opens too many windows", "writes more data into memory than the space allows", "prints a blank page"]'::jsonb,2,'Excess data spills into adjacent memory.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.D',4,'Buffer overflows can let attackers:','["speed up the network", "repair the program", "restore old files", "run their own code or crash the program"]'::jsonb,3,'Overflows can hijack execution.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.E',3,'Releasing an app with known security flaws can expose users to:','["data theft and loss of trust", "more storage", "free upgrades", "better reviews"]'::jsonb,0,'Insecure apps harm users.','original'),
('127.676.d.17.E',4,'A company that ships insecure software may face:','["lower scrutiny", "lawsuits, fines and reputation damage", "automatic awards", "guaranteed profits"]'::jsonb,1,'Insecure releases carry consequences.','original'),
('127.676.d.18.A',3,'In risk assessment, an asset is:','["a type of virus", "a bug report", "anything of value that needs protection", "a network cable only"]'::jsonb,2,'Assets are what you protect.','original'),
('127.676.d.18.A',4,'A written list of an organization''s hardware and software is an:','["index", "incident", "invoice", "inventory"]'::jsonb,3,'Inventories track assets.','original'),
('127.676.d.18.B',3,'Buying cyber insurance to shift financial loss to another party is risk:','["transference", "acceptance", "avoidance", "denial"]'::jsonb,0,'Transference passes risk to others.','original'),
('127.676.d.18.B',4,'Deciding not to offer a risky service at all is risk:','["acceptance", "avoidance", "mitigation", "transference"]'::jsonb,1,'Avoidance eliminates the activity.','original'),
('127.676.d.18.C',3,'A risk matrix ranks risks by comparing their likelihood and their:','["screen size", "color", "potential impact", "brand"]'::jsonb,2,'Matrices combine likelihood and impact.','original'),
('127.676.d.18.C',4,'Which scoring system is commonly used to rate the severity of software vulnerabilities?','["GPA", "BMI", "SAT", "CVSS (Common Vulnerability Scoring System)"]'::jsonb,3,'CVSS scores vulnerability severity.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
